    {
      "id": "claim_163fad30abd145cd8c0903b4ebc8925a",
      "statement": "The Account settings area (feature 076, src/screens/settings/account-settings-screen.tsx backed by src/hooks/use-account-deletion.ts) lets a user delete their own account, but only after a fresh re-authentication at Keycloak (prompt=login, max_age=0) that the BFF verifies server-side; on web the BFF builds the authorization request and owns the callback so the browser only sees a redirect URL, while on native the device runs its own expo-auth-session + PKCE flow (using a deletion-specific redirect distinct from the login callback) and posts the resulting code back to the BFF, and in neither case does the client itself perform the deletion.",
