    {
      "id": "claim_55efb57467ad443aae4a0240d0be0c7f",
      "statement": "Granting the Backups area's standing scheduled-run consent (src/hooks/use-backup-consent.ts) is a client-initiated, identity-provider-mediated round trip, not a local toggle: startGrant() only asks the BFF for a Keycloak authorization URL, the BFF itself records the grant after the user authenticates and Keycloak calls back, and revoke() surfaces an error and leaves the granted state unchanged (rather than optimistically clearing it) whenever the BFF reports that the identity provider refused the revocation.",
